I posted progress comments on the two issues this session's commits touched. I left both open and closed nothing. The build is passing; the fixes are committed locally, and the wrap-up step pushes them.

• **#1016 (comment posted, still open):** A test on the unfixed binary showed `kill -HUP` in the middle of a piped `-p` run left 0 of 18 streamed bytes on stdout. With c347aa34, SIGHUP now prints the held text and exits 129. A positive control showed the new SIGHUP test fails by name if the fix is removed. Of the other ways the process can end:
  • **SIGPIPE:** nothing is lost, because nobody is left reading.
  • **SIGKILL:** can't be caught, so the text can't be saved.
  • **SIGQUIT:** I measured it, and it still loses the held text.
  • **Panic:** not tested and not decided yet.

  The issue stays open for SIGQUIT and the panic case.
• **#869 (comment posted, still open):** Commit b3abc3ad settles how `/cd` deny-list checks are kept honest. A repo-wide test now fails if a `check_path` caller neither applies the `/cd` deny list nor appears on a named list of known gaps. It also fixes my earlier count: there were 6 unwired files, not 5. That commit wired up /goal, which leaves 5. /cd still doesn't reload permissions, hooks, MCP servers or skills.
